= Using the cronschedule class =

The [../classes/html/classcronschedule.html cronschedule class] provides methods for parsing a cron-style schedule string and determining whether a given date/time falls within that schedule.

A schedule is a string consisting of 5 space-delimited parts:

* year - eg. 2025, 2025-2027, 2025,2026, or *
* month - eg. 1, 1-6, 1,3,5, or *
* day-of-month - eg. 1, 1-15, 1,15, or *
* day-of-week - eg. 1, 1-5, 1,3,5, or *
* day-part - eg. 10:00, 9:00-17:00, 9:00-12:00,13:00-17:00, or *

Each part supports single values, lists, ranges, lists of ranges, and wildcards.

The schedule can be set as a single expression using setSchedule(), or each part can be set individually.  Once a schedule is set, isInSchedule() can be called with either a formatted date/time string or a datetime instance to determine if it falls within the schedule.

